{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-topological-mass-dilogarithm","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Conjecture","doco:Section"],"label":"conj:topological-mass-dilogarithm","kind":"conjecture","title":"Symmetric q-dilogarithm evaluation of exceptional-divisor contributions","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-topological-mass-holonomy","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-topological-mass-transient-localisation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-dilogarithm-disambiguation"],"tags":["quantum-dilogarithm","exceptional-divisor","briggs-klein","spectral-coordinates"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_dilogarithm_evaluation","text":"topological-mass-dilogarithm.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"conj:topological-mass-dilogarithm\"></a><p><em>Each exceptional-divisor summand evaluates to the symmetric <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-dilogarithm in the spectral coordinates of the Briggs--Klein chart at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_i</code>:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\bigl\\lVert\n  \\mathrm{MI}\\!\\!\\int_{E_i}\n  \\bigl(\\nabla_A q, L \\wedge F^+\\bigr)\n  \\bigr\\rVert\n  =\n  \\int_0^{z_i} \\frac{\\ln_q(1+t)}{t}\\, dt\n  =\n  -\\mathrm{Li}_2^q(-z_i).</code></pre>\n<p><em>Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Li}_2^q(z) = \\sum_{n \\ge 1} z^n/(n\\,[n]_q)</code> with the symmetric <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-integer <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[n]_q</code>. The series converges for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|z| &#x3C; q</code>; for other <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z_i > -1</code> both sides are meant by analytic continuation. The algebraic chart relation itself imposes no restriction on the domain of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z_i</code>. This is not the product <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q(z) = \\prod_{k\\ge1}(1-q^{-k}z)^{-1}</code>; see the <a href=\"#def:quantum-dilogarithm-disambiguation\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/magic-shells\">disambiguation</a>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-dilogarithm.md","heading":"Conjecture","number":"11.1.23","page":"b/conj-topological-mass-dilogarithm","qa":{"counts":{"pass":96,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":19,"unknown":0,"stale":103},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_dilogarithm_evaluation","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
